      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "A single continuous transformation shot. The scene starts exactly on <Picture 1> and lands exactly on <Picture 2>; treat the two frames as the same location, same subject, same lighting family, with only time passing between them.\n\n[0s-1.5s] Hold on the opening frame. Micro-motion only: air moves, light breathes, small details settle. The camera begins an almost imperceptible push-in.\n[1.5s-3.5s] The transformation carries the scene forward in one unbroken take. Volumes shift, colors migrate toward the closing palette, the light source drifts to its final position. No cuts, no dissolves, no morph artifacts.\n[3.5s-5s] Motion decelerates and the frame settles precisely into the composition of <Picture 2>, holding steady for the final beat.\n\nCamera: one continuous take, slow push-in easing to a full stop. No whip pans, no shutter cuts, no speed ramps.\n\nAudio: soft ambient room tone under the whole shot, a low rising swell that peaks near the midpoint, gentle textural detail as the transformation resolves, settling to near-silence on the closing hold. No narration, no music stings.\n\nPreserve subject identity and scene geometry from first to last frame. No flicker, no duplicated limbs, no text or watermarks.",
        1344,
        768,
        124
      ],
      "title": "MiniMax H3: First/Last Frame to Video"
    },
