        "## MiniMax H3 - FLF2V (open source)\n\n[MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) is MiniMax's omni-modal generation model. It generates video with **native stereo audio** - voice, SFX and music are modeled jointly in a single forward pass, not layered on afterwards. Up to 2K, 24fps, ~15s.\n\nThis graph is the **open-weights** path (`MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo`), not the paid `api_minimax_h3_flf2v` partner node. The checkpoint is literally `fl2va` = **f**irst/**l**ast frame **2** **v**ideo+**a**udio, so first/last-frame control is native - no extra module needed.\n\n## How to use\n\n1. **Load First Frame** -> the shot you start on.\n2. **Load Last Frame** -> the shot you end on.\n3. Write the prompt as a *timeline*, and refer to the keyframes as `<Picture 1>` (first) and `<Picture 2>` (last).\n4. Set **Resolution Selector** and **Float (duration)**, then run.\n\n**Both frames get center-cropped to width x height**, so give them the same aspect ratio as the Resolution Selector, or the ends will not match what you loaded.\n\nDropping the `last_frame` link turns this back into plain i2v; dropping both turns it into t2v. Same checkpoint, same graph.\n\n## Key inputs\n\n- **width / height** - H3's native canvas is a 768px short edge, capped at 768x1344, rounded to a multiple of 32. `16:9 @ 0.98MP` = 1344x768 is the native sweet spot.\n- **duration (seconds)** - the Math Expression converts it to a legal frame `length`: H3 samples on a 17-frame block grid (`17k + 5`) at 24fps. 5s -> 124 frames.\n- **steps** (Basic Scheduler) - 20 is the template default. Lower for drafts.\n- **seed** (RandomNoise) - fix it to iterate on a prompt without losing the take."
      ],
      "title": "Note: MiniMax H3 FLF2V",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
